SUMMARY:Panigiri of Taxiarchis\, Vathy
LOCATION:Vathy\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Vathy's whitewashed Taxiarchis monastery right on the beach celebrates twice a year\; the summer feast is on the evening of 12 July (Synaxis of Archangel Gabriel)\, with vespers\, then revithada and braised lamb at the monastery tables and a violin-and-laouto takimi. Same night the chapel of Ai-Silivestros on the Cheronissos road also celebrates. The village has a small car park\; many people come by boat from Kamares.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#vathy-panigiri-of-taxiarchis-vathy
